From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sky Malice <skym@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 07:50:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [upstream] [Gradle] Restore sourceSets in generate_gradle via
 flat collection.

In crrev.com/c/8261030, the per-target _GenerateGradleFile loop was
skipped in --all mode to avoid redundant template rendering.
However, this caused _all/build.gradle to have empty java.srcDirs,
res.srcDirs, and prebuilts because those global accumulator sets were
only populated during that loop.

Instead of running the expensive per-target generator.Generate loop
which redundantly scans directories and computes exclusions per target,
this collects the unique dependency closure in a single flat pass
directly inside _GenerateModuleAll.

This restores all sourceSets and prebuilts for the _all module while
retaining the time savings.

TAG=agy
CONV=30e1d7d6-ad4c-40a4-8614-15d3ee278679

Bug: 548551971
Change-Id: I3c4966ceeb45ec65c0d56405dd38ea0123ccaf9f
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8265278
Reviewed-by: Peter Wen <wnwen@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Sky Malice <skym@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1683146}
---
 build/android/gradle/generate_gradle.py | 58 ++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/android/gradle/generate_gradle.py b/build/android/gradle/generate_gradle.py
index 7b3f287a0ef20..050574db45b9c 100755
--- a/build/android/gradle/generate_gradle.py
